# What Aries may depend on: every module go.mod requires directly, every
# tool the gate runs, and every GitHub Action a workflow uses (AGENTS.md,
# rule 4; docs/design/supply-chain.md, §7.2). internal/depcheck fails
# when go.mod, internal/tools/pin/go.mod, the link sets of aries,
# ariesd and sextant or the workflows name something this file does not,
# or this file names something they do not. sextant has no scope of its
# own: it runs beside ariesd and links ariesd's telemetry, so it may link
# what ariesd may (internal/depcheck, linksAs).
#
# One line each, fields separated by spaces:
#
#   path  scope  license  since  reason
#
# path     a module's path, or an Action's owner/repo (a subpath, such as
#          actions/cache/restore, is the same repository at the same commit)
# scope    which may link or run it: aries, ariesd, both (the binaries),
#          tools (the gate's tools and tests only) or actions (workflows)
# license  the SPDX identifier of the license its files carry; several,
#          separated by commas, when each covers some of its files. What
#          aries or ariesd links is Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause,
#          ISC, MIT or MPL-2.0 (decision 82)
# since    the day it was first taken, YYYY-MM-DD
# reason   why the standard library would not do, to the end of the line
#
# A person adds a line, in the pull request that adds the dependency; an
# agent may propose one and never adds it. An indirect module needs no
# line: it is held to the link sets in internal/depcheck/testdata.
#
# Programs that are not Go modules (shellcheck and apparmor_parser from
# the runner's Ubuntu, Postgres from its project's apt repository, whose
# key ci.yml checks) are not listed here; mise.toml and internal/version
# pin what they can.

# The agent interface.
github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk  aries  Apache-2.0,MIT  2026-10-06  the MCP server aries mcp speaks; the protocol's own SDK
github.com/google/jsonschema-go  aries  MIT  2026-10-06  the JSON schemas of the MCP tools, as the MCP SDK takes them

# The store.
github.com/jackc/pgx/v5  ariesd  MIT  2026-10-15  the Postgres driver; the standard library has none (decision 79)

# Telemetry, ariesd's alone (design §16.2, decision 28).
go.opentelemetry.io/otel  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  OpenTelemetry's API: spans and attributes (design §16)
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  OpenTelemetry's trace API
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/metric  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  OpenTelemetry's metric API
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/log  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  OpenTelemetry's log API, for log records over OTLP
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  OpenTelemetry's SDK: the tracer provider and its batching
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  the SDK's meter provider and readers
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/log  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  the SDK's logger provider
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  OTLP/HTTP push of spans
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlpmetric/otlpmetrichttp  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  OTLP/HTTP push of metrics
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlplog/otlploghttp  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  OTLP/HTTP push of log records
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/prometheus  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  the instruments in Prometheus's format on /metrics
go.opentelemetry.io/contrib/instrumentation/runtime  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  the Go runtime's metrics (memory, goroutines, GC)
github.com/prometheus/client_golang  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  the /metrics handler and registry the Prometheus exporter writes to
github.com/go-logr/logr  ariesd  Apache-2.0  2026-10-12  otel.SetLogger takes a logr.Logger: how the SDK's own errors reach ariesd's log

# Both binaries.
go.yaml.in/yaml/v3  both  MIT,Apache-2.0  2026-10-06  .aries.yaml and ariesd's config; the standard library parses no YAML
golang.org/x/crypto  both  BSD-3-Clause  2026-10-06  SSH, client and server; the standard library has Ed25519 but no SSH
golang.org/x/sys  both  BSD-3-Clause  2026-10-06  the Windows console's modes for aries tui (internal/board), which syscall lacks; x/crypto and others link it in both
golang.org/x/term  aries  BSD-3-Clause  2026-10-08  raw mode and the terminal's size, for aries tui and prompts

# Tools the gate runs.
golang.org/x/vuln  tools  BSD-3-Clause  2026-10-06  govulncheck, pinned by internal/tools/pin/go.mod and its go.sum
# The one tool go.sum does not cover: golangci-lint/golangci-lint-action
# installs its binary by the version string ci.yml pins (docs/design/
# supply-chain.md, §11), and mise.toml the same version for contributors.
github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/v2  tools  GPL-3.0  2026-10-06  the linters the gate runs (.golangci.yml); run, never linked

# GitHub Actions, each pinned by a 40-character commit with its version
# in a comment.
actions/checkout  actions  MIT  2026-10-06  checks the repository out in every job
actions/setup-go  actions  MIT  2026-10-06  installs the Go of go.mod's toolchain line
actions/cache  actions  MIT  2026-10-13  restores and saves the module and build caches (ci.yml)
actions/attest-build-provenance  actions  MIT  2026-10-07  the release archives' build provenance
actions/upload-artifact  actions  MIT  2026-10-07  hands the release's archives from build to sign-and-publish
actions/download-artifact  actions  MIT  2026-10-07  takes them in sign-and-publish
golangci/golangci-lint-action  actions  MIT  2026-10-06  installs and runs golangci-lint at its pinned version
github/codeql-action  actions  MIT  2026-10-07  CodeQL's analysis (codeql.yml)
